{
  "summary": "Handles socket error conditions in the P2P network loop and HTTP server separately from read events. When `poll()` reports socket errors or hangups on connections where reads are not currently requested, the node disconnects immediately instead of attempting an I/O operation that would inevitably fail. It also adds functional test coverage for TCP urgent data handling and peer resets while sending.",
  "problem": "When socket polling reports an error condition on a connection whose reads are paused, the node attempts a write (or read in HTTP) that subsequently fails and triggers a disconnect anyway. This produces inaccurate log messages and redundant failed I/O calls.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'If errorSet is reported for a socket we did not request to read from, disconnect directly instead. This just adds clarity: previously it would attempt a send that would then fail. The only side-effect is a changed log message.'",
    "Commit 582840ae83: 'Disconnect directly on POLLERR/POLLHUP when no read was requested, skipping the send attempt that would otherwise fail and disconnect the peer.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36716"
    ],
