  "card": "Disconnects sockets immediately when poll() reports error or hangup events on connections where reads were not requested, rather than attempting a doomed send or read first. This applies to both the P2P networking loop and the HTTP server, avoiding redundant failed I/O operations and clarifying debug log output upon disconnection. It also expands test coverage for TCP urgent data handling and peer resets during send stalls. Depends on PR #36716.",
